g themselves up properly."], [15.6, 17.48, "So here's what happens to your airways"], [17.48, 21.12, "if you slide two capture cards under your mattress and pillow"], [21.12, 23.06, "and leave them there for four weeks."], [23.44, 25.38, "Slide them in, that's the whole job."], [25.7, 27.14, "The first night while you sleep,"], [27.14, 30.16, "the lure starts drawing dust mites up out of the foam."], [30.46, 32.76, "The one's building up two inches under your face."], [33.06, 35.18, "That's the plant-derived pheromone lure,"], [35.44, 37.26, "pulling them away from the place you breathe"], [37.26, 38.52, "for eight hours a night."], [38.76, 41.06, "By the end of week one, most people find"], [41.06, 42.54, "they're not reaching for a tissue"], [42.54, 43.8, "the second they sit up."], [43.98, 46.42, "That's because every mite the lure pulls out"], [46.42, 49.74, "stops dropping its 20 pellets a day of Derpy 1"], [49.74, 50.82, "where your face sleeps."], [51.2, 53.3, "The allergen that breaks down the junctions"], [53.3, 55.06, "holding your airway lining together."], [55.06, 57.9, "Week two, you stop wondering if you're coming down"], [57.9, 60.46, "with something and that clearer by lunch feeling"], [60.46, 61.84, "starts showing up at breakfast."], [62.28, 65.9, "That's the adhesive, locking every mite the lure pulls in"], [65.9, 68.32, "so what it catches comes out of your bed"], [68.32, 69.74, "instead of back into it."], [69.96, 72.56, "The craziest part, you haven't sprayed a thing."], [72.78, 74.06, "You haven't stripped the bed."], [74.32, 75.72, "You haven't bought a new mattress,"], [76.06, 77.46, "but every single night,"], [77.72, 80.04, "the mattress you sleep on is giving them up."], [80.24, 83.36, "Week four, by now most people are sleeping through more"], [83.36, 85.14, "and waking up less blocked."], [85.42, 87.36, "Mornings start the way they did years ago"], [87.36, 90.8, "and that background dread before you even open your eyes"], [90.8, 94.48, "is finally gone for you and for whoever shares your bed."], [94.8, 95.86, "How is this possible?"], [96.22, 98.14, "Most mite products try to kill them,"], [98.4, 100.46, "but every dead one stays in the bed"], [100.46, 102.98, "carrying the same allergen as a live one."], [103.24, 105.02, "This one pulls them out alive."], [105.46, 106.86, "Dust mites have no eyes."], [107.14, 109.54, "They find each other by scent, a chemical signal."], [109.82, 111.72, "Capture cards mimic that signal,"], [111.72, 113.54, "drawing them up out of the foam"], [113.54, 115.42, "and the adhesive locks them on."], [115.72, 117.0, "It's lure and trap."], [117.3, 119.66, "The way pest control has caught things for decades"], [119.66, 122.2, "aimed at the one place nobody had,"], [122.5, 123.8, "the inside of a mattress."], [124.22, 126.54, "Because a dead mite can't walk to a card."], [126.82, 129.56, "Over 30,000 homes are already pulling them"], [129.56, 132.06, "out of their beds instead of washing around them"], [132.06, 134.72, "up to 65% off right now"], [134.72, 137.0, "with a 90 day money back guarantee."], [137.36, 137.96, "Tap below."]]}